<p>Bulgarians voted on Sunday to choose the 240 members of the National Assembly, the latest national ballot in the repeat-election cycle that has gripped the Black Sea nation since 2021. Opinion polls cited by several outlets put former president Rumen Radev and his soft-euroskeptic Progressive Bulgaria coalition ahead, though not by enough to guarantee a majority, pointing to another round of difficult coalition talks after the vote. The vote comes after the previous government collapsed in December following mass protests, extending a stretch in which fragile administrations have repeatedly failed to last. For many Bulgarians, this election is a test of whether the country can finally break out of weak governance and political churn.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/DTmBdjTXX9Ta-Y61eqAjHUi8TOEFNsIQLj0DdpOoW5lMwphoSxD40XziujzF7KvPGZ-rv_BZ6neuHACi8PFMrtMiQ2WB_w9M6Y2wKvgQawWryeqMBWv2aSpYH2kQ-JGa8302z-KSyt00KkA265Shz4Wxd4UCdfzUafIBUrahLB9aMWH_XruM6HHDg4iPrp9Ju-KWCp8XdVbBlqdQjkn3spmqNKmvfg' alt='Former President Rumen Radev of Bulgaria speaking during the last pre-election event of his coalition, Progressive Bulgaria.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Population scale: The election is unfolding in a country of about 6.5 million people, underscoring how deeply the long-running deadlock has weighed on one of the EU’s smaller member states.</li><li>Durability test: Since 2021, no Bulgarian government has lasted more than a year, so staying power may matter almost as much as the seat count on election night.</li><li>How governments fall: Recent cabinets have fallen to both street protests and backroom deals in parliament, showing that instability has come from pressure outside the chamber as well as maneuvering inside it.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Rumen Radev and Progressive Bulgaria: Outlets describe Radev’s coalition as soft euroskeptic, left-leaning, or pro-Russian, making foreign-policy alignment one of the clearest fault lines in the race. (<a href='https://apnews.com/article/bulgaria-election-radev-borissov-corruption-russia-427c265d8b314a00fbbcd159b76b52e2'>Associated Press</a>, <a href='https://www.dw.com/en/bulgarians-vote-in-high-stakes-election/a-76846189'>DW</a>, <a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/bulgaria-votes-as-pro-russian-former-president-leads-the-polls'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Boyko Borissov and established parties: Borissov remains a major competitor, showing how familiar political figures still anchor Bulgarian politics despite years of churn and failed coalition-building. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/bulgarians-vote-in-high-stakes-election/a-76846189'>DW</a>)</li><li>Bulgarian voters: The New York Times describes many voters as yearning for the more prosperous life enjoyed in other parts of Europe, showing how economic hopes sit behind the ballot alongside party rivalry. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/19/world/europe/bulgaria-elections-what-to-know.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Corruption debate: AP includes corruption among the issues hanging over the contest, suggesting the election is also a test of whether any coalition can rebuild trust in public institutions. (<a href='https://apnews.com/article/bulgaria-election-radev-borissov-corruption-russia-427c265d8b314a00fbbcd159b76b52e2'>Associated Press</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/bulgarians-vote-in-high-stakes-election/a-76846189'>Bulgarians vote in high-stakes election</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/19/world/europe/bulgaria-elections-what-to-know.html'>What to Know About the Bulgarian Election</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.youtube.com/watch'>Bulgaria heads to the polls in eighth general election in five years • FRANCE 24 English</a> - youtube.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/19/bulgarians-head-to-polls-to-elect-parliament-for-eighth-time-in-5-years'>Bulgarians head to polls for eighth time in five years</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/bulgaria-votes-as-pro-russian-former-president-leads-the-polls'>Bulgaria votes as pro-Russian former president leads the polls</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/bulgaria-parliamentary-elections-rumen-radev-april-19-2026-updates/article70880075.ece'>Bulgarians head to the polls to elect a parliament for the eighth time in 5 years</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://apnews.com/article/bulgaria-election-radev-borissov-corruption-russia-427c265d8b314a00fbbcd159b76b52e2'>Bulgarians vote for 240 seats of the National Assembly in the nation&#x27;s eighth election since April 2021. Former president Rumen Radev leads the soft eurosceptic Progressive Bulgaria coalition, the frontrunner of the election according to opinion polls. (AP)</a> - apnews.com</li></ul>